Now that the priest is angry, may as well take him out and then
pay the price afterwards.  Priests have one fatal weakness - They
always stay on the altar or adjacent to it.  That means they are
vulnerable to missile attack even if they are wearing a [oMR not a
robe to make them immune to your MM spell.

> I've been struggling to figure out how to play a Wizard and am excited
> with how far I've gotten on this run. =A0Can I do anything to make the
> Priest happy? =A0Can I dispose of him without upsetting my God so I can
> still get my gift?

The price of taking out a priest isn't all that high.  Depending on
your alignment it's loss of telepathy, loss of protection, loss of
luck, loss of alignment points.  At this point you don't have
protection to worry about.  The luck is handled by sacrafice.
The alignment is handled by killing hostiles and/or sacrafice.
The telepathy is handled with missiles and another floating eye
or if you want to get crowned.

